        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કિલ્લો (killo) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic qalʿa, \"a fortress\". It is masculine: જૂનો કિલ્લો, an old fort."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
